      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find \\(ab + ac + bc\\) for the roots \\(a, b, c\\) of the polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a cubic polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n\\[\na + b + c = -\\frac{b}{a},\n\\]\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a},\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = -\\frac{d}{a}.\n\\]\n\nIn the given polynomial \\(3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0\\), the coefficients are \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -3\\), \\(c = 11\\), and \\(d = -8\\). We need to find \\(ab + ac + bc\\).\n\nUsing the formula \\(ab + ac + bc = \\frac{c}{a}\\), we substitute the values of \\(c\\) and \\(a\\):\n\\[\nab + ac + bc = \\frac{11}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(ab + ac + bc\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{11}{3}}\\).",
